      "writtenOn": "2024-09-19T18:54:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so this is the current design:\n\n1) always enable SkAvifCodec in Android framework build (i.e.) both `SkAvifCodec` and `SkHeifCodec` will be registered.\n2) at runtime, based on the system property `media.avif.crabbyavif`, we will pick between `SkAvifCodec` and `SkHeifCodec`. essentially, if the flag is set, the `SkAvifCodec` will return true for `IsAvif`, otherwise it will always return false and we will fall back to `SkHeifCodec` for AVIF images.\n\nOne more thing to note is that we also need to know whether we are using `SkHeifCodec` or `SkAvifCodec` when creating the SkAndroidCodec because one uses SkAndroidCodecAdapter and the other uses SkSampledCodec since they handle scaling differently. so we need to use the right adapter depending on which decoder is being used for a given image.",
      "parentUuid": "5b0b0d8f_ca3346c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 15,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 65
