      "message": "Using a #define to control what implementation of a given codec is compiled in is no longer an approved way to do things in Skia.\n\nWhat I think we should do to structure this better is:\n1) extract the bits of SkAvifCodec.cpp/.h that are agnostic to the avif-codec impl into something like SkAvifCommonCodec.cpp/.h\n2) Move the parts of the current avif impl to SkAvifCodec_libavif.cpp (or whatever the current impl is called).\n3) Add the CrabbyAvif impl parts to SkAvifCodec_crabby.cpp (or something similarly named).\n4) Duplicate include/codec/SkAvifDecoder.h to include two new, nested namespaces `SkAvifDecoder::LibAvif` and `SkAvifDecoder::Crabby`. Keep the existing namespace `SkAvifDecoder` returning the libavif version\n5) Android Framework should compile/link/register the Crabby version when it\u0027s supported.",
