      "message": "Thanks for the detailed suggestions.\n\nRegarding 1-4 - the only reason we added AVIF support to `SkAvifCodec` via `libavif` was to use it in Android. It is not used anywhere else (the original plan was to use `libavif` on Android but it was veto\u0027ed by security so we pivoted to `CrabbyAvif`). So there is no real need to continue to retain the `libavif` based `SkAvifCodec` implementation. So would it be okay if i simply replace `SkAvifCodec` to use `CrabbyAvif` (so that we would not have any of the `#define` trickery? The downside to that is that we cannot test it in standalone skia builds until https://g-issues.skia.org/issues/312495780 is resolved.\n\nRegarding 5 - i will look into registering codecs on the Android side. From Leon\u0027s other comment, it seems like this is currently not being done on Android and it uses whatever the old/default behavior is. My knowledge of how skia is used from the Android framework is quite limited and i don\u0027t know how large of a change this is. I will take a look at it next week and update this thread.",
