      "side": 1,
      "message": "Registration was added (somewhat) recently by @kjlubick@google.com. I believe `SkCodec::Register` is what you want. I *thought* we had updated clients (e.g. Android), but I haven\u0027t found the right code.\n\nIf we don\u0027t already register them (which seems to be the case), I would probably put the registration in [`init_android_graphics`](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/6bdb46de484fc9a90f1ac96866cce0ce3a4975cd:frameworks/base/libs/hwui/apex/jni_runtime.cpp;l\u003d163;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0), and perhaps wherever else we call `SkGraphics::Init`. Then we can read the property once to determine which one to register. (We\u0027ll need to register all of the other decoders Android uses already; I think maybe we have a fallback path that Android relies on right now?)",
