      "writtenOn": "2024-09-24T21:39:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i looked into the Android code and it seems like we are using the default list that is in `SkCodec::get_decoders_for_editing`.\n\nThe avif codec is registered there like so:\n```\n#ifdef SK_CODEC_DECODES_AVIF\n            decoders-\u003epush_back(SkAvifDecoder::Decoder());\n#endif\n```\n\nif i can update that code to:\n```\n#if defined(SK_CODEC_DECODES_AVIF)\n#if defined(SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK)\n            if (property_get_int32(\"media.avif.crabbyavif\", 0) !\u003d 0)\n#endif // defined(SK_BUILD_FOR_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK)\n                decoders-\u003epush_back(SkAvifDecoder::Decoder());\n#endif\n```\n\nThat is all i need to get the desired behavior without having to change the way Android registers codecs with skia. I really feel like updating the way Android registers all codecs with skia is outside the scope of what i am trying to do here. I don\u0027t have enough knowledge on the graphics stack to even deal with breakages because of that should some arise.\n\nSo would it be okay if i update this CL to make this change? This way I can remove the `AvifEnabled()` function.",
